# AUB Secure Files

ALL user/person/internal files are private by default.

DO NOT use the public disk for student, teacher, parent, staff, or any other person-related files.
DO NOT create direct `/storage` URLs for those files.
DO NOT create a new file storage path outside `SecureFileService`.
DO NOT put a bearer token in a file URL.
DO NOT trust filename extensions or client MIME types.
DO NOT store raw uploaded child photos without server-side decode/re-encode.

If a new feature needs a file:

1. Register an explicit category in `config/aub-files.php` (unknown category = DENY).
2. Store and replace only through `App\Services\SecureFiles\SecureFileService`.
3. Serve only through `/secure-files/{uuid}` (web) or `/api/v1/files/{uuid}` (mobile, Sanctum).
4. Authorize through `FileAccessService` (actor + attachable + category + action). Unknown relation/category = DENY.

This applies to future report cards, consent, messaging, productions, payments, teacher documents, and anything else with personal or internal data.

Public disk is allowed only for genuine public website assets (logo, CSS/JS, marketing). Never turn private/person content into a public asset.

Details: `docs/en/Security/Secure_Files.md`.
